            {
                "entry_id": "71b98fe5-5849-3d25-9f03-2bac44e36038",
                "word": "Madonna",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0f8fb163-0db7-4f11-8156-f4610f040013",
                        "entry_id": "71b98fe5-5849-3d25-9f03-2bac44e36038",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Madonnas"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6c8b564c-d978-3371-b17a-9857951786fd",
                        "entry_id": "71b98fe5-5849-3d25-9f03-2bac44e36038",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An artistic representation of the Virgin Mary, chiefly when holding the infant Jesus."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "490e9cb5-bf74-4411-9494-16d1fcda18f3",
                                "sense_id": "6c8b564c-d978-3371-b17a-9857951786fd",
                                "text": "A beautiful example of this type of Madonna is the polyptych in the Museo Civico in Sansepolcro."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e1c990c-c7ee-40d3-a989-b8cfe22c0d56",
                                "sense_id": "6c8b564c-d978-3371-b17a-9857951786fd",
                                "text": "So many Madonnas were produced during the Renaissance that it became the habit to distinguish them by any peculiarity."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bfea2f52-befe-399b-9e05-24bca916fdbe",
                        "entry_id": "71b98fe5-5849-3d25-9f03-2bac44e36038",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A morally pure woman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a638234-5be4-4be2-b869-5583169500dd",
                                "sense_id": "bfea2f52-befe-399b-9e05-24bca916fdbe",
                                "text": "“Men,” I said, with a tone of disgust. “Halal circles, haram circles, good, bad, Madonnas, whores, goats, penises, it’s all the same.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a314e798-0183-4db8-a9b3-9b567954eb60",
                                "sense_id": "bfea2f52-befe-399b-9e05-24bca916fdbe",
                                "text": "[…] the mothers who, like Sebastian’s mother in Notorious or Mitch’s mother Lydia in The Birds, block such a transference, or by potential love-objects who are, themselves, Madonnas, whores, or otherwise thinly disguised maternal figures."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "21fc4f14-8647-4835-a10c-cbcb033fc7c0",
                                "sense_id": "bfea2f52-befe-399b-9e05-24bca916fdbe",
                                "text": "The Madonnas are the mothers to our children, the pillars of our families, and the goddesses of our communities. The Madonnas shun the dark side of human sexuality and banish the whores to hell. We put the Madonnas on a pedestal, and we can’t think of them as being sexual or sexy because they must be pure. They must be virginal like the Madonna herself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3db1a74b-51d5-4268-85d3-9c7407ce675e",
                                "sense_id": "bfea2f52-befe-399b-9e05-24bca916fdbe",
                                "text": "Sparing no one in her response to her interviewer’s questions about the ERA, she alludes to divisions within the women’s movement, referring to the factions as “Madonnas, whores, housewives, and lesbians.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bdea761f-381e-42f1-9226-75cdcb224646",
                                "sense_id": "bfea2f52-befe-399b-9e05-24bca916fdbe",
                                "text": "In sexual politics the view of women as either Madonnas or whores limits women’s sexual expression, offering two mutually exclusive ways to construct a sexual identity."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "4027d39d-3ef9-3c27-9b54-638ab00ff30d",
                "word": "madonna",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "097cfda7-dad6-4005-a614-cf83eba441ce",
                        "entry_id": "4027d39d-3ef9-3c27-9b54-638ab00ff30d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "madonnas"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e2ed1986-c0a5-3663-a7f3-2e8894e9d4ee",
                        "entry_id": "4027d39d-3ef9-3c27-9b54-638ab00ff30d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative letter-case form of Madonna.",
                            "A representation of the Virgin Mary."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e0b8605-77fb-4e45-8533-3508bb11215c",
                                "sense_id": "e2ed1986-c0a5-3663-a7f3-2e8894e9d4ee",
                                "text": "Glogau Stat.—Inns: Deutsches Haus; Westphal’s Hotel. A fortress of the 2nd rank on the l. bank of the Oder, 17,000 Inhab. The Dom upon an island dates from 1120, and contains a madonna by Cranach, sen., his masterpiece."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d4c07e5-c2d1-4899-bf23-f2806a401dda",
                                "sense_id": "e2ed1986-c0a5-3663-a7f3-2e8894e9d4ee",
                                "text": "Giacomo Medica’s (1965) sample of the 697 most important Marian sanctuaries in Italy gives us some idea of the number of Italian madonnas in Italy as a whole."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e2b3e16-15ae-4832-ad23-663059463a56",
                                "sense_id": "e2ed1986-c0a5-3663-a7f3-2e8894e9d4ee",
                                "text": "When it has not whitened them, the church has attempted to assimilate dark or black madonnas; this is evident in the many Italian madonnas described as bruna."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "27c59f23-ee12-4fc5-9590-d47273a542c3",
                                "sense_id": "e2ed1986-c0a5-3663-a7f3-2e8894e9d4ee",
                                "text": "The darkening effects of being buried, especially outdoors, sounds plausible in a few such cases, but if candle smoke is to account for all the other dark madonnas, as the Church asserts, why would not the entire statue have become black?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a58dcddf-0079-317f-baa3-073df70df328",
                        "entry_id": "4027d39d-3ef9-3c27-9b54-638ab00ff30d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative letter-case form of Madonna.",
                            "A morally pure woman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "34a5bc4c-1696-4e05-a043-26b9cdc4664d",
                                "sense_id": "a58dcddf-0079-317f-baa3-073df70df328",
                                "text": "Yet most of us will probably deny that this blissful woman is a sexual woman. We associate her with Virgin Mary, who conceived in an act of spiritual purity and not in carnal lust and desire. We regard her chastity as essential to her maternal rectitude. Thus we hardly recognize the madonna's subtle sensuality as sexual energy, especially not in an age where we measure sexuality in orgasmic potency."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "38a3d4cb-0b9f-4c4f-ba9c-1ab8d0039a29",
                                "sense_id": "a58dcddf-0079-317f-baa3-073df70df328",
                                "text": "For centuries, madonnas provided legitimate children and social respectability; whores, illegitimate pleasure."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3944b162-4695-4342-acb6-3ba70973b454",
                                "sense_id": "a58dcddf-0079-317f-baa3-073df70df328",
                                "text": "[…] whether women’s liberation might be better achieved by rejecting the traditional dichotomization of women into good girls/bad girls, madonnas/whores, and hence refusing to organize one's sexual desire and pleasure in terms of the repressive and passive roles that are traditionally ascribed to female sexuality within dominant discourses (the so-called ‘agency’ model)."
